rules:
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture decisions must be recorded and updated only in ADR; all other
    representations must be derived from ADR.
  title: Rule Adr Single Source Of Truth
- id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: AEM must remain consistent with ADR decisions and must not contradict them,
    while still able to include vision, roadmap, and architectural direction.
  title: Rule Aem Consistency With Decisions
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture Work is the authoritative source for architectural planning
    state; generated artifacts must derive planning status from Architecture Work
    rather than maintaining independent state.
  title: Rule Architecture Work Authority
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Core patterns must represent foundational architectural primitives, not
    specific strategies or implementations.
  title: Rule Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All decisions must use a structured YAML decision schema rather than unstructured
    narrative, enabling machine processing and consistent interpretation.
  title: Rule Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Lifecycle stage must be derived from decision status; proposed maps to
    NEXT or REVIEW, accepted may map to DONE, rejected must not be active, and deferred
    maps to FUTURE or DEFER.
  title: Rule Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All architectural decisions must be persisted as structured ADR before
    being reflected in AEM or other artifacts.
  title: Rule Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Patterns must not be merged or consolidated across different architectural
    layers.
  title: Rule Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Generated governance artifacts must summarize authoritative sources and
    must not become authoritative sources themselves.
  title: Rule Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Heuristic-derived patterns must include at least one linked signal as evidence.
  title: Rule Heuristic Patterns Require Signals
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Foundational global semantic contract for architecture artifacts, defining
    distinctions among intent, decisions, system state, pattern status, lifecycle
    terminology, and consistent usage.
  title: Rule Language Semantic Contract
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Pattern maturity and decision lifecycle must be interpreted consistently
    without conflation, following decision-status-driven stage rules.
  title: Rule Pattern Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All patterns must be created as supporting by default and never directly
    as core.
  title: Rule Patterns Born As Supporting
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: 'Rule conflicts resolve by precedence: global rules above project rules,
    and project rules above prompt rules; higher-precedence rules must be applied.'
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Pattern promotion to core requires strong evidence, preferably from multiple
    sources or systems.
  title: Rule Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Projects must participate in a shared Knowledge Workspace and must not
    duplicate existing workspace-level governance structures.
  title: Rule Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Signals may be promoted to patterns only when recurrence, system impact,
    reusability, stability, and supporting evidence criteria are all satisfied.
  title: Rule Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architectural decisions must be proposed by the system and explicitly accepted,
    rejected, or deferred by an architect.
  title: Rule System Proposes Architect Decides
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Runtime-native workflows must conform to the CAS Workflow Execution Model,
    preserving separation among orchestration, knowledge access, workflow reasoning,
    and schema validation.
  title: Rule Workflow Execution Model Compliance
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
